================================================================================
=== WEB-PARITY MAP (components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx -> native) ===
================================================================================
  props open/title/message/confirmLabel/cancelLabel/variant/loading/
    requireTypedConfirmation/typedConfirmationLabel/silenceKey/onConfirm/onCancel
                                              -> ConfirmRequest + ConfirmDialogController seam
  variantToSeverity {danger:critical, warning:warn}   -> ConfirmDialogProjection.severity(for:)
  iconComponents {AlertOctagon, AlertTriangle}        -> ConfirmSeverity.iconSystemName
       (exclamationmark.octagon.fill / .triangle.fill)
  severityTokens[sev] bg/border/fg                    -> ConfirmSeverity.tone + message block chrome
  silenceHonored (key && variant!=danger && !typed)   -> ConfirmDialogProjection.silenceHonored(...)
  typedMatches / confirmDisabled = loading||!match     -> .typedMatches / .confirmDisabled
  reset typed + dontAskAgain on (re)open               -> model.resetFormIfNewRequest(...)
  open && silenced -> onConfirm() + render null        -> autoResolve -> visibility .hidden + confirm
  Esc / backdrop -> onCancel unless loading            -> model.dismiss()  (swallowed while busy)
  handleConfirmClick (persist silence then confirm)    -> model.confirm()  (async, submitting flag)
  inputLabel = typedConfirmationLabel ?? `Type "X"…`   -> ConfirmDialogProjection.typedConfirmationLabel
  lib/confirmSilence.ts isSilenced/silence (localStorage,
    key teslasync:confirm-silence:v1)                  -> ConfirmDialogSilenceStore (+ UserDefaults impl)
  useTranslation t('confirm.silence.checkbox', …)      -> ConfirmDialogStrings (P1/S10, "ConfirmDialog")

  States reproduced (every one renders real chrome — engineering guideline #6, never a blank box):
    loading (request resolving) | empty (nothing to confirm) | error (delivery failed + retry)
    | content (the confirm form) | inline-error (cached request + failed reload)
    | freshness chip Live/Stale/Offline + cached-data banner (ADR-013)
    | in-flight submitting (web `loading`: buttons disabled + confirm spinner)

Collision-safety (rule 9): every public type is `Confirm…`/`ConfirmDialog…`-prefixed and was checked
  unique across the whole module BEFORE writing. The shared confirm-silence registry already exists
  under generic names in unrelated surfaces (ConfirmSilenceStore in PrivacySection;
  UserDefaults/InMemoryConfirmSilenceStore in AdvancedSettings), so ours were named
  ConfirmDialogSilenceStore / UserDefaultsConfirmDialogSilenceStore /
  InMemoryConfirmDialogSilenceStore to avoid a duplicate-type collision. No shared file touched.

